pr_comments:
> This offers a new printf variant which cuts out a bunch of format modifier support while allowing us to add long long support to the 'regular' variant while still offering something smaller.

@keith-packard Could you please try out `samples/subsys/logging/dictionary` code sample?
I've noticed that it seems to be broken with picolibc (but also newlib, IIRC) and I wonder if this PR would by any chance make the situation better and/or be an opportunity to address other outstanding issues around format modifiers. Thank you!

review_comments:
I would be ok filtering-out individual checks as long as he minimal config isn't the default.

```cpp
if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PICOLIBC_IO_MINIMAL)) {
  ztest_test_skip();
}
```

After all, users would explicitly be choosing to use a format that is trimmed-down, maybe non-standard, discards things, etc.

